.TH SDL_IsAudioDevicePhysical 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_IsAudioDevicePhysical \- Determine if an audio device is physical (instead of logical).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_IsAudioDevicePhysical(SDL_AudioDeviceID devid);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
An
.BR SDL_AudioDeviceID
that represents physical hardware is a physical device; there is one for each piece of hardware that SDL can see\[char46] Logical devices are created by calling
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDevice
or
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream ,
and while each is associated with a physical device, there can be any number of logical devices on one physical device\[char46]
.PP
For the most part, logical and physical IDs are interchangeable--if you try to open a logical device, SDL understands to assign that effort to the underlying physical device, etc\[char46] However, it might be useful to know if an arbitrary device ID is physical or logical\[char46] This function reports which\[char46]
.PP
This function may return either true or false for invalid device IDs\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I devid
the device ID to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if devid is a physical device, false if it is logical\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

